    <patterns>
      <pattern name="highest-wins read composition" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs">GroupBy(...).Max(AccessLevel) at :945-950 and :993-1000 is what makes a write-side level reduction observable as an effective-access reduction. ConfersAccessOn at :124-125 is the in-memory mirror of the read filter's own expiry predicate.</pattern>
      <pattern name="request-independent survivor election" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalGrantLifecycle.cs">ElectSurvivor / ConferralRank take NO request value (task 106), which is what lets the conferral check speak for the whole key. EffectiveExpiry at :187-188 answers a per-request question and must not be used to rank rows.</pattern>
      <pattern name="refusal writes nothing" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/SetRecordShareExpiryEndpoint.cs">The sibling endpoint's refusal paths are the shape to copy: every 4xx/5xx branch returns before any write, and its tests assert _bulkUpdates is empty ("a refused request writes nothing", RecordShareExpiryTests.cs:243).</pattern>
    </patterns>
